WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
Milan, in the year 390.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.820
News arrives of a
massacre at Thessalonica.

3
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.880
The bishop of Milan refuses
the emperor communion,

4
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.090
until he does public penance.

5
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.960
Yet the same Christian scriptures
tell believers to pray for kings,

6
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.580
and to honour the king.

7
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.780
So should a church obey
the government, guide it,

8
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.460
or stand against it?

9
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:26.500
In this mission, you'll trace church and
state from Rome's emperors to Irish kings,

10
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.430
penal laws and modern constitutions.

11
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.820
Then you'll weigh up
the lessons of history,

12
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:35.910
from the slave trade to peace
talks in Rome and Northern Ireland.

13
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.710
Your mission: weigh up how a
church should relate to the state.
